# The build context for tools/container/Dockerfile, and only for it. BuildKit
# reads the ignore file that sits beside the Dockerfile it was given before it
# falls back to the one at the context root, and the one at the context root
# sends only evals/ and src/: it belongs to the evaluation images, which want a
# context of a few hundred kilobytes.
#
# Written the way the repository root's own ignore file is written: nothing
# goes, and what the build needs is named back in. The other direction, naming
# what to leave out, is a list that cannot keep up, and this one had already
# fallen behind every path this repository's .gitignore marks as local
# machine-bound state, so a build from a working checkout carried the builder's
# bench configuration, the agent loop directory, the local agent configuration
# and both caches into a layer. The next local directory somebody creates would
# have gone the same way.
**

# What the image installs and what it runs. The four files and src/ are what
# the tests build their wheels out of, requirements/ is the locked dependency
# set the image installs, and tests/ is the tier itself.
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!MANIFEST.in
!requirements
!src
!tests

# And not what a build leaves behind inside those.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
